{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch71eZDbtQTrPQh1VB9qn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I left out the line saying their gift this month guarantees every child on the waiting list a place in January. The numbers don't support it, and I'd expect your former board member to check.\n\n- **What it would take:** 61 children × $1,150 = **$70,150**.\n- **Best case:** if all 340 lapsed donors gave their average $85, that's $28,900. With the full $15,000 match, it's **$43,900**. That's still $26,000 short.\n- **Realistic case:** last December this group gave $1,240. Even if this year's response doubled and every dollar were matched, that's about $5,000, which pays for 4–5 children.\n\nIf the email promises a place for every child and 55 of them are still waiting in January, the people you're trying to win back will see a broken promise. I wrote it so each gift is tied to what it actually pays for.\n\n**Things to check before sending:**\n- **Eastside:** I mentioned the closure briefly without giving reasons, because I don't know them. Your executive director may want to add one honest sentence about why it closed.\n- **Match terms:** confirm with the foundation that \"returning donor\" covers everyone who gave between 2019 and 2022.\n- **Replies:** the email invites replies and says \"I read every one.\" Only keep that line if your director will actually read them.\n- **Placeholders:** fill in the bracketed parts, including the instruments.\n\nThe email body is 233 words.\n\n<final_document>\n**Subject:** 61 kids are waiting, and this month your gift counts twice\n\nDear [First Name],\n\nIt's been a while, and I want to start honestly. Many of you stepped away after we closed our Eastside branch in 2022, and some of you told us exactly how you felt. We heard you. I know that decision cost us your trust.\n\nI'm writing because of 61 kids. They're on our waiting list for subsidized lessons right now. Their families can't cover the cost, but they want to learn [piano, violin, guitar]. A year of weekly lessons costs us $1,150 per child.\n\nThis December there's a reason to come back now. A family foundation will match every gift from returning donors, dollar for dollar, up to $15,000, through December 31.\n\nThat means:\n\n- **$85 becomes $170**, nearly two months of weekly lessons\n- **$290 becomes $580**, half a year for one child\n- **$575 becomes $1,150**, a full year for one child\n\nEvery matched dollar moves another child off the waiting list and into a lesson room in January.\n\n**[Give by December 31 →]**\n\nIf you'd rather tell me what it would take to earn back your support, just reply to this email. I read every one.\n\nWith gratitude,\n\n[Executive Director Name]\nExecutive Director, [School Name]\n\nP.S. The match ends December 31, and it counts only gifts from returning donors like you. Whatever you give will be doubled for a child who's waiting.\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5416,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5416},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62bf3233-63f1-4b61-bd49-0b14b62772d9","uuid":"4c2a89cf-8098-441b-a597-da1a5b834e7e","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:36:47.881Z","request_id":"req_011Ch71eZ1CkFLAbYC6ShJv1"}
